Suppose your university is conducting a survey to collect students’ opinions of online classes. You are to write a response to the survey about their advantages and disadvantages, 
and what improvements can be made.


##
  Nowadays, taking online classes has become a common phenomenon. Opinions vary from person to person. As far as I am concerned, taking online classes have its advantages and 
disadvantages.
	For one thing, online classes bring convininence and much available time for us. At home and the lesson will start soon, we can open our computer quickly to involve in class. 
It is not needed to get in class in person. However, it also has disadvantages when bringing us convininence. Some students may just turn on their computer and at the same time, 
they spend time to doing another things.
	From my perspective, when taking online classes, professor can ask students to open photographer, making sure professor can know the status of students. Only in this way can
let students focus on the lesson.


## 逐处错误标注
1. taking online classes **have** → **has**
动名词短语作主语，谓语用单数
2. convininence → **convenience**（拼写错误）
3. involve in class → **join the class** （join 表示参与课程；involve 多用于被动 be involved in）
4. spend time to doing → spend time **doing**（固定搭配）
5. another things → **other things**；another + 单数名词，other + 复数名词
6. professor → **professors**（泛指，用复数）
7. open photographer → **turn on their cameras**
photographer 是 “摄影师”；camera 才是摄像头，用词错误
8. Only in this way can let… 句式错误
only 倒装结构不能直接加 let，改为 Only in this way can students…


## 修正版本
  Nowadays, taking online classes has become a common phenomenon. Opinions vary from person to person. As far as I am concerned, taking online classes **has** its advantages and 
disadvantages.
  For one thing, online classes bring **convenience** and more flexible time for us. When a class is about to start at home, we can quickly turn on our computer to join the class.
There is no need to attend class in person. However, online learning also has drawbacks while bringing us convenience. Some students may just turn on their computers and do
other things at the same time.
  From my perspective, professors can require students to turn on their cameras during online classes so that they can check students’ learning state. Only in this way can 
students concentrate on the lessons.


##优化完整版
  Nowadays, taking online classes has become a common phenomenon. Opinions vary from person to person. As far as I am concerned, taking online classes has both advantages and
disadvantages.
  For one thing, online classes bring great convenience and flexible time. We can attend courses at home without travelling to classrooms. For another, online learning has obvious
weaknesses. Without strict supervision, some students are easily distracted and do other things instead of listening carefully.
  From my perspective, teachers can take some measures to improve online courses. For example, they may ask students to turn on cameras and raise questions frequently. Only in 
this way can students stay focused and gain better learning results.


